PATCH 114: reconstruct the MAINMENU box+items sprite-blit path (260c clip + 26a1 dispatch + 26de blit)
and thread the c6b4 draw call.

e9f0 (MAINMENU per-frame paint) draws the gray menu box + 7 item labels via one sprite blit:
    mov ax,0x13d8 ; mov bx,0xf790 ; lcall [DGROUP:0x6b4]     (DGROUP:0x6b4 = MGAVIDEO 0x26a1)
ax=0x13d8 = the box sprite's byte offset into the MSPRITE6.BIN sprite directory (DGROUP:0x4f0);
bx=0xf790 = the position/rect descriptor {row0=62,col0=111,row1=161,col1=209}.  Three driver functions
were base-lost by Ghidra:

- FUN_0000_260c (sprite CLIP calc, asm 0x260c..0x265f): dropped the sprite-directory indirection
  `mov si,ax; mov es,[0x4f0]; les si,es:[si]; mov ax,es:[si-4]` (read the sprite-id AX as an already-
  resolved host far-ptr -> NULL deref), the DGROUP bases of the position/clip descriptors, and never
  returned ES:SI (the record far-ptr) or CF/ZF.  Reconstructed to resolve the record via the directory
  and publish ES:SI + CF (clipped-out) + ZF (word[clip]==0xa000) to shim statics.  ALSO: the clip result
  words DGROUP:0x1588..0x158e are 16-bit, but the Ghidra _DAT_1000_d58X macros are undefined4 (4-byte)
  and their stores OVERLAP (d588's dword zeroes d58a's high half, d58c's zeroes d58e) -> wrote them as
  uint16_t.  (Without this the column came out 0 and the box rendered at the left edge / wrapped.)
- FUN_0000_26a1 (blit dispatcher, asm 0x26a1..0x26dd): used in_CF/in_ZF=0 locals, dropped 260c's ES:SI,
  and read the clip coords from the wrong DGROUP base.  Reconstructed to branch on 260c's real CF/ZF and
  read [0x1588]/[0x158a] at g_mem+0x1d588/0x1d58a (DGROUP:0x1588, not 0x1c588); ZF path runs 2d6d + the
  row-table setup then blits.
- FUN_0000_26de (masked sprite blit, asm 0x26de..0x2757): dropped the fb-dest ES base, the source
  DS(=sprite seg) base, and mis-typed _DAT_1000_c724 (host deref).  Rebuilt the bases (dest =
  word[[0x724]][0] : rowtab[row]+col ; source = recseg:recoff ; stride = word[[0x724]+4]^cx-cx), reading
  the source seg from the 260c static; the 3 blit modes (RLE type-2 / odd-aligned / even) are the Ghidra-
  recovered arithmetic, unchanged.

Also thread e9f0's [0x6b4] far-vector call with ax=0x13d8 / bx=0xf790.  Result: the gray box + 7 item
sprites blit to 0xA0000, centred at the reference position.  Asm-verified 0x260c..0x2757, 0x26a1..0x26dd,
0xe9f9.
